.TH TUI_DIALOG_FORM_INIT 3 2026-11-15 "libtuikit 1.4" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_dialog_form_init, tui_dialog_form_free, tui_dialog_form_handle,
tui_dialog_form_render \- a form in a modal frame
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/fieldset.h>
.PP
.BI "int  tui_dialog_form_init(tui_dialog_form *" d ", const char *" title ,
.BI "                          const char *" hint ", tui_fieldset *" form );
.BI "void tui_dialog_form_free(tui_dialog_form *" d );
.BI "tui_dialog_state tui_dialog_form_handle(tui_dialog_form *" d ", const tui_event *" ev );
.BI "void tui_dialog_form_render(tui_dialog_form *" d ", tui_canvas " c );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A
.BR tui_fieldset (3)
in a centred box with a frame: the
.I title
in the top border and a key
.I hint
in the bottom border.
.I hint
may be NULL, which gives
.B TUI_DIALOG_FORM_HINT
(" Tab next  Enter OK  Esc cancel ").
Like every dialog it neither blocks nor reads the terminal: the program gives it
events and draws it last.
.PP
.BR tui_dialog_form_init ()
copies the title and the hint and keeps the pointer to
.IR form ,
which the caller owns and frees (with
.BR tui_fieldset_free (3))
after
.BR tui_dialog_form_free ().
It returns 0, or \-1 with
.B EINVAL
(no dialog or no form) or
.BR ENOMEM .
The members
.I frame
and
.I fill
(styles; the scheme's frame and text roles) may be set afterwards.
.PP
.BR tui_dialog_form_handle ()
passes one event to the form and returns its state: the keys of
.BR tui_fieldset_handle (3),
Enter submits through the form's
.I validate
(a refusal shows its reason inside the frame and the dialog stays open), Esc
and Ctrl-C cancel.
The outcome, too, is
.IR form\->state :
.B TUI_DIALOG_OK
or
.BR TUI_DIALOG_CANCELLED .
.PP
.BR tui_dialog_form_render ()
draws the box centred in
.IR c ,
sized to the fields (the widest label and value, the title, the hint), to the
completion drop-down's rows when a field completes, and to one row for the error,
and at most to the canvas less a margin of one cell.
The cursor goes to the focused text field.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tui_fieldset_init (3),
.BR tui_dialog_message (3)
